## Band Description

Brittle Psalm Works is a five-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around the principle that the space after a plucked phrase can carry more arrangement information than the phrase itself.

**Selam Tesfaye** — krar, pentatonic cells, damping, open-string resonance, phrase spacing.

**Jonah Vale** — illbient drums, tape loops, sub architecture, Shadow Interval arrangement.

**Mekdes Alemu** — prepared pump organ, uneven reed drones, suspended harmonic afterbodies.

**Noah Price** — bass trombone, breath pedals, half-valve smears, muted low-mid emergence.

**Dawit Bekele** — frame drum, dry transient substitution, finger rolls, muted bass strokes.

There is no conventional frontperson. Selam defines the audible edges of the composition; Jonah arranges the contaminated space between them; Mekdes gives selected gaps sustained harmonic weight; Noah briefly stabilizes the low-mid field; and Dawit makes specific electronic positions physical. Live versions vary because every Shadow Interval can breathe differently while the krar cycles remain structurally fixed.

